  ▐ aura  Done. Summary of the task:

**The bug** — `io.fits.FITSDiff` on a file compared with itself raised `ValueError: The truth value of an array with more than one element is ambiguous` (a false "difference") whenever the file had **Q-format** VLAs (`QD`/`QI` columns). P-format VLAs (`PD`) diffed clean.

**Root cause** — in `astropy/io/fits/diff.py`, `TableDataDiff._diff` (line 1452) routed VLA columns through a per-row comparison only when `"P" in col.format`; Q-format columns fell through to `np.where(arra != arrb)`, which raises on `_VLF` object arrays.

**The fix** (one line, source only, left uncommitted in the working tree):
```python
elif "P" in col.format or "Q" in col.format:
```
This matches exactly what the newer system astropy does for the same code.

**Verification** (project root `C:/Users/agent/work/work/astropy-14539_panel`, run with `C:/Python312/python.exe3` after building extensions in place):
- Before the fix: QD/QI self-diffs raised `ValueError`; after: `QD_only`, `QD_plus`, `QI_plus`, `PD_plus` and the repo's `variable_length_table.fits` all report `identical=True`, `diff_total=0`.
- `pytest astropy/io/fits/tests/test_diff.py -q` → **48 passed**.

